      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nconst candidates = $('Discover RSS Candidates').all();\nconst blogUrl = $('Extract Blog URL').first().json.blog_url;\n\n// Collect RSS responses with their candidate URLs\nconst feeds = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n  const data = items[i].json.data || '';\n  const error = items[i].json.error?.message || '';\n  const url = candidates[i]?.json?.rss_url || 'unknown';\n  if (data && typeof data === 'string' && data.length > 50) {\n    feeds.push({ url: url, content: data.substring(0, 3000) });\n  }\n}\n\n// Get blog page HTML as fallback\nlet html = '';\ntry {\n  const pageData = $('Fetch Blog Page').first().json;\n  html = (pageData.data || '').substring(0, 12000);\n} catch (e) {}\n\nreturn {\n  blog_url: blogUrl,\n  feeds: JSON.stringify(feeds, null, 2),\n  html: html\n};"
      },
      "id": "81ed842a-22d9-45de-9972-37e82eddd1e5",
      "name": "Prepare Feed Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        9248,
        2760
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are determining the most recent blog post date for '{{ $('Get Vendor Record').first().json.company_name }}'.\n\nBlog URL: {{ $json.blog_url }}\n\nI fetched several potential RSS/Atom feed URLs. Here are the responses:\n\n{{ $json.feeds }}\n\nYour task:\n1. Check each feed response. A VALID post feed must:\n   - Be RSS or Atom XML (not an HTML error page)\n   - Contain actual <item> or <entry> elements with post content (not just <channel> metadata)\n   - NOT be a comment feed (WordPress comment feeds have titles like \"Comments on: ...\" and no <item> elements)\n2. If you find a valid post feed, extract the most recent <pubDate>, <published>, or <updated> date from the items.\n   Also return the URL of the feed that worked as blog_rss_url.\n3. If NO valid RSS/Atom feed was found among the candidates, use this blog page HTML instead to find the most recent post date:\n\n{{ $json.html }}\n\n   When reading HTML, scan ALL visible dates and return the MOST RECENT one.\n   Do not use copyright years, footer dates, or non-post metadata.\n\nReturn blog_rss_url as the working feed URL (or null if you used HTML instead).\nReturn latest_post_date in YYYY-MM-DD format, or null if no date was found.\nReturn confidence as \"high\" (clear date from RSS), \"medium\" (date from HTML), or \"low\" (uncertain).",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
